<!-- ============ EXTENSIVE FUNCTIONALITY ============ -->
<section class="section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Extensive Functionality</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Systems Teamwork Commerce integrates with.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Teamwork Commerce connects to external platforms across ERP, warehouse management, analytics, shipping, marketing, traffic counters, returns automation, third-party marketplaces, fraud detection, CRM, accounting, and internal legacy systems, including live integrations with SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics, and NetSuite.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="pillars-grid" style="grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);">
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-building-warehouse"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">ERP, warehouse &amp; fulfillment</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Live ERP integrations with SAP, Oracle, Microsoft Dynamics, and NetSuite, alongside warehouse management and returns automation, connected directly to POS, so fulfillment can be managed and monitored from the point of sale with the notifications and visibility to keep it optimized.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-credit-card"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">Payments & fraud</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">A variety of payment processing integrations let retailers take payments across every channel, including contactless in store, payment by link, and online checkout, alongside fraud detection built into the flow.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-mail"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">Marketing & CRM</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Integrated platforms like Klaviyo and Mailchimp drive audience growth and content engagement, alongside CRM and customer communication tools that keep customers informed through fulfillment.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-chart-line"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">Analytics</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Analytics integrations, backed by a dedicated data analytics and machine learning team, turn transaction data into the kind of data-oriented insight that's hard to get from POS data alone.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-device-desktop"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">In-store hardware</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Cash drawers, receipt printers, customer displays, feedback tools, and traffic counters all connect to POS, so the point of sale stays the hub of the in-store experience, not one piece of it.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pillar-card">
        <div class="pillar-icon"><i class="ti ti-building-bank"></i></div>
        <h3 class="pillar-title">Marketplaces & accounting</h3>
        <p class="pillar-desc">Third-party marketplace connections and accounting integrations tie into the same backend as everything else, including the internal legacy systems many retailers still depend on.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ CLOUD NATIVE INFRASTRUCTURE ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Cloud Native Infrastructure</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Built on Google Cloud.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Running cloud-native removes the infrastructure, maintenance and data centre costs a retailer would otherwise carry, and means new platform services arrive without a hardware project.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 44px; align-items: center;">
      <div class="cloudx">
        <div class="cloudx-layer">
          <i class="ti ti-device-ipad"></i>
          <div><strong>The store</strong><br><span>iOS devices, peripherals, RFID readers</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cloudx-layer is-core">
          <i class="ti ti-brand-google"></i>
          <div><strong>Teamwork Commerce on Google Cloud</strong><br><span>POS, OMS, inventory, RFID, reporting, one codebase</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="cloudx-layer">
          <i class="ti ti-plug-connected"></i>
          <div><strong>Your systems</strong><br><span>ERP, WMS, e-commerce, payments, CRM</span></div>
        </div>
        <p class="cloudx-note">Other providers, including AWS, Azure and Tencent, and hybrid deployments, are supported by request.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0 0 16px;">The store talks to one platform. The platform talks to everything else. Nothing in the middle for you to run, patch or capacity-plan.</p>
        <p style="font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.75; color: var(--text-muted); margin: 0;">Because the platform is cloud-native rather than hosted, new capabilities ship into the same deployment you already have rather than arriving as an upgrade project.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- ============ ARCHITECTURE & INTEGRATION TEAM ============ -->
<section class="section" style="padding-top: 0;">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Architecture</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">Add or change integrations without downtime.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">Omnichannel ecosystems change constantly. Integrations attach to the platform rather than being wired through it, so one can be replaced while the rest of the estate keeps trading.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="swapx" role="img" aria-label="One integration detaching from the platform core while a replacement connects, with the core continuing to run.">
      <div class="swapx-side">
        <span class="swapx-chip"><i class="ti ti-building-warehouse"></i> ERP</span>
        <span class="swapx-chip"><i class="ti ti-credit-card"></i> Payments</span>
        <span class="swapx-chip is-out"><i class="ti ti-plug-off"></i> Legacy WMS</span>
